                <invention-title lang="de">ABSCHWÄCHUNG EINES BRUTE-FORCE-ANGRIFFS AUF VORRICHTUNGS-PIN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">ATTÉNUATION D'ATTAQUES DE FORCE BRUTE SUR UNE BROCHE DE DISPOSITIF</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">MITIGATION OF BRUTE FORCE ATTACK ON DEVICE PIN</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method and system for device authentication are disclosed. A user device receives a password from a user and generates a transaction signing key or one-time password (OTP) master key based on the password and at least one secret provided by an authentication device. Using the derived key, the user device generates a signed secure transaction or OTP, which is transmitted to the authentication device. The authentication device validates the received data without indicating invalid password attempts and grants access to a secure resource only upon successful validation. In some embodiments, the authentication device transmits updated secrets to the user device after successful verification, allowing resynchronization and continued protection of the signing key. Also disclosed are a user device comprising a processor and memory configured to execute the authentication method, and a non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions to perform the method, thereby mitigating brute force or oracle attacks.</p>
            </abstract>
